config DRM_S7D
	tristate "Amlogic S7D display controller and HDMI transmitter (experimental)"
	depends on AMLOGIC_C5_DISPLAY_RESOURCES
	depends on DRM && I2C && AMLOGIC_CPU_INFO
	depends on DMA_CMA && REGMAP_MMIO
	depends on !AMLOGIC_MEDIA_ENABLE
	select PHY_MESON_S7D_HDMI
	select RESET_S7D_VPU
	select DRM_KMS_HELPER
	select DRM_GEM_DMA_HELPER
	select DRM_DISPLAY_HELPER
	select DRM_DISPLAY_HDMI_HELPER
	select DRM_BRIDGE_CONNECTOR
	select SND_SOC_HDMI_CODEC if SND_SOC
	help
	  Build the S7D VPU execution path and HDMI transmitter bridge, with
	  DRM EDID/SCDC helpers, CCF consumers and generic PHY ownership.
	  Built in or as the module s7d-drm. Unbinding stops the output and
	  frees its resources; buffers the hardware may still read after a
	  failed stop are leaked.
	  Register one CRTC, a linear RGB primary, VD1/VD2 video planes and
	  shared OSD2 cursor/overlay planes, an HDMI connector and a VDIN1
	  writeback connector. NV12/NV21 primary framebuffers scan out on VD1.
	  Cursor and RGB overlay cannot be visible together; the cursor takes
	  ARGB8888 up to 256x256. Video is progressive NV12/NV21/NV16/NV61,
	  UYVY/VYUY, VUY888 or XVYU2101010 with BT.601/709/2020
	  limited/full-range conversion; VD1 also reads 8- and 10-bit 4:2:0
	  Amlogic FBC decoder frames.
	  Each local OSD scaler supports up to 4x enlargement and 2:1 reduction,
	  including simultaneous primary and RGB overlay scaling. Linear RGB
	  scaling requires opaque pixels and input width up to 3840.
	  VD1 supports up to 4x enlargement and 8x downscaling up to UHD
	  output, skipping source lines where a reduction would outrun the
	  fetch. Linear video and OSD scaling may run together within a checked
	  combined clock budget. VD2 uses independent classic PPS for sources
	  up to 2048x1080.
	  The primary takes compressed framebuffers only with
	  s7d_drm.primary_afbc=1, as switching it between compressed and
	  linear or YUV framebuffers takes a modeset. Mali AFBCD reads ABGR8888
	  in the tiled 32x8 layout and ARGB8888/XRGB8888 in the untiled one,
	  on a primary or OSD2 overlay up to 4096x2160, with opaque global
	  alpha and optional premultiplied pixel alpha.
	  AFBC scaling uses the same local OSD limits and uncropped source.
	  An AFBC primary can use a linear OSD2 cursor or
	  overlay. Mali AFBCD can decode the primary and the OSD2 overlay together
	  (no cursor), up to 3840x2160 decoded pixels in total; adding or
	  removing one of them requires a stopped modeset. An AFBC primary can
	  combine with VD1 and VD2 up to 1080p at 148.5 MHz while only VD1
	  scales, and only to enlarge; joint primary/video changes require a
	  stopped modeset. FBC video does not combine with compressed graphics.
	  Interlaced 1080i, 480i and 576i output takes linear OSD planes only.
	  Supports S7D revision B, with TMDS up to 594 MHz. Takes over a firmware
	  output when there is one; otherwise starts the display from reset.
	  Do not enable with legacy media/display writers. System sleep, including
	  deep sleep where firmware powers the display domain off, restores the
	  output. Before the first commit, sleep is refused while a firmware
	  output still runs.
	  HDMI PCM uses SND_SOC_HDMI_CODEC with the Amlogic AXG sound card
	  (SND_MESON_AXG_SOUND_CARD). Cold HDMI SRAM initialization is not
	  supported.

config DRM_S7D_GFCD
	bool "S7D GFCD compressed primary plane (experimental)"
	depends on DRM_S7D
	help
	  Use GFCD for AFBC primaries that Mali AFBCD cannot read
	  (XBGR8888), and for ABGR8888 with the GFCD primary policy. Supports
	  ABGR8888 and XBGR8888 in the 32x8 tiled AFBC layout, with framebuffers
	  up to 4096x2160, width aligned to 32 and height aligned to 8.
	  Integer source windows up to 1920x1080 at 148.5 MHz are supported.
	  XBGR8888 always ignores X and uses opaque pixels. The local
	  OSD1 scaler supports up to 4x enlargement or 2x reduction into a
	  1920x1080 output with opaque pixels, subject to the core clock budget.
	  Unscaled ABGR8888 also supports premultiplied alpha.
	  GFCD also reads RGBA8888 AFRC primaries (SCAN layout, coding unit
	  16, 24 or 32 bytes) with dimensions aligned to 64x16, within the
	  same window, scaler and alpha limits and without reflection.
	  Linear or Mali AFBCD OSD2 overlays remain available; video and
	  simultaneous GFCD surfaces are excluded. GFCD primaries need
	  s7d_drm.primary_afbc=1.
	  Requires the retained GFCD automatic clock and reset configuration.
	  Keep disabled to use only the Mali AFBCD backend.

choice
	prompt "S7D AFBC primary decoder policy"
	depends on DRM_S7D
	default DRM_S7D_AFBC_POLICY_MALI
	help
	  Select which decoder reads an ABGR8888 AFBC primary, offered with
	  s7d_drm.primary_afbc=1. The s7d_drm.afbc_policy parameter (0 Mali,
	  1 GFCD) overrides it.

config DRM_S7D_AFBC_POLICY_MALI
	bool "Mali AFBCD"
	help
	  Decode every ABGR8888 AFBC plane with Mali AFBCD, S0 for the
	  primary and S1 for the OSD2 overlay. GFCD only reads XBGR8888 AFBC
	  and AFRC.

config DRM_S7D_AFBC_POLICY_GFCD_PRIMARY
	bool "GFCD within its envelope"
	depends on DRM_S7D_GFCD
	help
	  Decode an AFBC primary up to 1920x1080 at 148.5 MHz with GFCD,
	  leaving Mali AFBCD S1 for the OSD2 overlay.

endchoice
